@flexiarg operator/start-with-the-smaller-mode-first
@title Start With The Smaller Mode First
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 4 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade; THEN worded 4 ways across its proposals
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-8N1Ph6 turn-GnZeXU turn-MDwJCW turn-kuEWAB
@parent operator/commission-the-smallest-reviewable-act
@context A build has more than one mode and the operator has to pick where to begin.

! conclusion: Build only the named mode, record design decisions, and stop at a point he can review before the next mode.

  + IF:
    He says to work on one of them first.

  + HOWEVER:
    The agent may take the go-ahead as covering all modes, or settle design questions the operator wanted to see.

  + THEN:
    Build only the named mode, record design decisions, and stop at a point he can review before the next mode.

  + BECAUSE:
    A scoped first mode gives a checkable result before the rest is spent.
